 "_comment": "Round 64, feature 6: the data-use declaration (policy_context.data_use) every SDK checks before sending, as the server checks it (orchestrator internal/api/policy_gate.go checkDataUse and checkClient, internal/pepg/psl/round64.go), and the keyed reference helper. A code is ^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._:-]{0,63}$ matched against the whole text (a trailing newline is refused). purpose and basis are required codes; categories is a list of at most 20 distinct codes; reference, when present and not empty, is hmac-sha256: and 64 lowercase hex digits; an empty reference or an empty categories list is a value left out, as the server reads it. No other key is accepted. The reference helper computes hmac-sha256: and the lowercase hex HMAC-SHA256 of the identifier's UTF-8 bytes under the customer's key (key_hex, at least 32 bytes) on the customer's own machine, so the identifier itself never leaves it; it refuses a shorter key or an empty identifier. client_name and client_version in attested_context are at most 128 bytes of printable ASCII (0x20 to 0x7e) with no leading or trailing space; an empty value is one left out. Verdifax seals each declaration as made and does not check it. Every SDK reads this file in a test.",
